这三位正处于巅峰状态的喜剧演员。

936
00:39:50.880 --> 00:39:51.980
I mean, brilliant.
我是说，太绝了。

937
00:39:52.360 --> 00:39:55.680
We had another fan question from Evan Derrickson.
我们还有另一个粉丝提问来自埃文·德里克森。

938
00:39:55.680 --> 00:39:57.420
This is a technical question.
这是一个技术问题。

939
00:39:57.680 --> 00:40:02.840
Evan wants to know who got to decide who wears which mustache because they're really perfect
埃文想知道是谁决定谁戴哪种胡子的，因为它们真的跟每个角色绝配，

940
00:40:02.840 --> 00:40:04.760
for each character and so funny.
而且太搞笑了。

941
00:40:04.960 --> 00:40:06.280
Is that a wardrobe thing?
这是服装部门负责的吗？

942
00:40:06.560 --> 00:40:07.920
Does it need Greg's approval?
需要经过格雷格的批准吗？

943
00:40:08.200 --> 00:40:09.080
Is it props?
是道具吗？

944
00:40:10.220 --> 00:40:14.440
Well, Evan, I like your question because you've clearly been listening to Office Ladies.
好吧，埃文，我很喜欢你的问题，因为你显然一直在听《办公室女士》播客。

945
00:40:14.440 --> 00:40:18.160
The mustaches are made by hair and makeup.
胡子是由发型和化妆部门制作的。

946
00:40:18.220 --> 00:40:19.540
So it's not a prop.
所以这不是道具。

947
00:40:19.940 --> 00:40:25.640
And hair and makeup work together because it's hair, because it's a mustache, right?
而且发型和化妆会一起合作，因为它是毛发，因为它是胡子，对吧？

948
00:40:25.740 --> 00:40:25.880
Yeah.
对。

949
00:40:25.880 --> 00:40:28.860
But then it goes on the face and has to be applied to the face.
但它要贴在脸，必须上妆固定在脸上。

950
00:40:28.900 --> 00:40:30.900
So it becomes a makeup thing.
所以这就变成了化妆部门的事。

951
00:40:31.180 --> 00:40:35.180
So they just had a tray of a bunch of different mustaches.
所以他们当时弄了一盘各种各样的小胡子。

952
00:40:35.180 --> 00:40:37.580
And yes, they got Greg's approval.
而且没错，他们得到了格雷克的批准。

953
00:40:37.780 --> 00:40:39.360
They talked to Joss Whedon, the director.
他们跟导演乔斯·韦登谈过。

954
00:40:39.360 --> 00:40:44.300
They talked to Mindy Kaling, and they picked the mustaches for each of these guys to wear.
他们跟敏迪·卡灵聊过，然后为这里的每个人挑了要戴的小胡子。

955
00:40:44.580 --> 00:40:50.600
Hair and makeup would take photos of the guys with the different mustaches and then walk
发型和化妆团队会给戴着不同小胡子的男演员们拍照，然后走过去

956
00:40:50.600 --> 00:40:52.800
them over to the writer's room.
拿到编剧室去。

957
00:40:52.800 --> 00:40:55.060
And the writers and directors would look at it.
然后编剧和导演们会过目。

958
00:40:55.120 --> 00:40:55.880
I can't imagine.
我简直无法想象。

959
00:40:56.160 --> 00:40:57.320
That is so funny to me.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

960
00:40:57.760 --> 00:41:00.560
Well, next up, the Finer Things Club meeting is underway.
好吧，接下来，高雅俱乐部正在开会。

961
00:41:01.280 --> 00:41:01.800
Yes.
没错。

962
00:41:01.800 --> 00:41:06.620
And at 10 minutes, 50 seconds, we have a Pam's teapot catch.
在10分50秒的时候，我们捕捉到了帕姆的茶壶。

963
00:41:07.020 --> 00:41:08.800
Yes, that's right.
对，没错。

964
00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:15.060
They are using Pam's teapot that Jim gave her in that very first Christmas episode.
他们用的是吉姆在第一集圣诞节送给帕姆的那个茶壶。

965
00:41:15.180 --> 00:41:18.020
I have a question for the Finer Things Club.
我有个问题想问高雅俱乐部。

966
00:41:18.420 --> 00:41:18.860
Yes.
请说。

967
00:41:19.040 --> 00:41:23.440
How much stuff do you have to bring to work on the day that you guys meet?
你们聚会那天得带多少东西来上班啊？

968
00:41:23.440 --> 00:41:32.380
There is a three-tiered tray of sandwiches, a tablecloth, flatware, the teapot, the cups.
有三层三明治盘、桌布、餐具、茶壶、茶杯。

969
00:41:32.900 --> 00:41:35.760
You're like bringing a crate of stuff.
你们简直像是搬了一箱东西来。

970
00:41:36.320 --> 00:41:36.560
Yeah.
对啊。

971
00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:38.120
Don't worry about it.
不用操心。

972
00:41:38.800 --> 00:41:40.300
It doesn't involve you.
这跟你没关系。

973
00:41:40.500 --> 00:41:41.220
We got it covered.
我们都准备好了。

974
00:41:41.520 --> 00:41:46.060
They're discussing a room with a view and who walks in but Andy.
他们正在讨论《看得见风景的房间》，结果谁进来了，是安迪。

975
00:41:46.420 --> 00:41:47.780
He wants to be in the club.
他想加入这个俱乐部。

976
00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:51.020
And Pam tells him it's a closed club.
然后帕姆告诉他这是个封闭的俱乐部。

977
00:41:51.800 --> 00:41:56.260
She's very direct and unapologetic.
她非常直接，一点也不委婉。

978
00:41:56.260 --> 00:41:57.040
I'm sorry.
不好意思。

979
00:41:57.280 --> 00:41:58.680
This is a closed club.
这是个封闭的俱乐部。

980
00:41:59.020 --> 00:42:05.380
And Andy has a talking head where he says the Finer Things Club is the most exclusive club in the office.
然后安迪有一段单人访谈，他说高雅俱乐部是办公室里最排他的俱乐部。

981
00:42:05.520 --> 00:42:07.600
So it's naturally where he needs to be.
所以他自然而然就得加入。

982
00:42:08.320 --> 00:42:10.600
Party planning committee is his backup.
聚会筹划委员会是他的备选。

983
00:42:11.200 --> 00:42:12.600
Kevin's band is his safety.
凯文的乐队是他的安全网。

984
00:42:14.160 --> 00:42:16.380
Everything is like he's rushing a fraternity.
一切搞得就像他在参加兄弟会纳新一样。

985
00:42:16.720 --> 00:42:17.940
It's so true.
太真实了。

986
00:42:18.280 --> 00:42:19.260
It's so true.
真的是这样。

987
00:42:19.260 --> 00:42:22.640
Well, I'll have you know, we loved shooting these scenes.
好吧，我不妨告诉你们，我们拍这些戏时可喜欢了。

988
00:42:22.900 --> 00:42:24.560
Me, Oscar, Paul.
我、奥斯卡、保罗。

989
00:42:24.800 --> 00:42:26.640
We were delighted by the storyline.
我们对这个故事情节感到很高兴。

990
00:42:26.900 --> 00:42:31.180
We had the best time because this was a group of people that did not normally get to hang out.
我们度过了最美好的时光，因为这是一群平时根本没机会聚在一起的人。

991
00:42:31.340 --> 00:42:33.680
I did not have a lot of scenes with Oscar or Paul.
我和奥斯卡或保罗没多少对手戏。

992
00:42:33.800 --> 00:42:35.420
So this was really cool.
所以这真的很棒。

993
00:42:35.620 --> 00:42:41.540
And I'll have you know that before the pandemic, we had a Finer Things Club reunion lunch.
而且我得告诉你们，在疫情之前，我们还举办过一次高雅俱乐部的重聚午餐。

994
00:42:41.720 --> 00:42:42.480
You did.
你们聚过啊。

995
00:42:42.520 --> 00:42:45.100
I thought this was so, so sweet.
我觉得这真的太贴心了。

996
00:42:45.100 --> 00:42:48.480
When you told me you guys were all going to meet, I was like, that is adorable.
你跟我说你们要聚会的时候，我觉得这太可爱了。

997
00:42:48.980 --> 00:42:49.160
Yeah.
对啊。

998
00:42:49.300 --> 00:42:49.820
We met.
我们见面了。

999
00:42:49.920 --> 00:42:50.560
We had lunch.
我们吃了午饭。

1000
00:42:51.100 --> 00:42:52.580
And we invited Ed.
而且我们邀请了埃德。

1001
00:42:52.840 --> 00:42:53.140
Oh.
哦。

1002
00:42:53.660 --> 00:42:54.520
We let Ed come.
我们让埃德也来了。

1003
00:42:56.140 --> 00:42:58.420
So the four of us had this amazing lunch.
所以我们四个人吃了顿超棒的午餐。

1004
00:42:58.560 --> 00:43:00.340
I took a picture, so I'll post it in the pod.
我拍了张照，打算发到工作群里。

1005
00:43:00.560 --> 00:43:01.600
That is so sweet.
太贴心了。

1006
00:43:01.600 --> 00:43:05.320
I'm very sad I wasn't invited on the show or in real life.
我没能被邀请上节目，现实中也没被邀请，我好难过。

1007
00:43:05.480 --> 00:43:10.280
Well, I'll say we did not discuss any literature or art at our reunion lunch.
好吧，我得说我们在聚餐时根本没讨论什么文学或艺术。

1008
00:43:10.280 --> 00:43:13.120
We just chatted about our lives and our kids.
我们只是闲聊了各自的生活和孩子。

1009
00:43:13.700 --> 00:43:14.040
Aw.
噢。

1010
00:43:14.440 --> 00:43:17.660
Well, now the guys have rolled up to the Utica branch.
好了，现在这帮男人们已经到了尤蒂卡分公司。

1011
00:43:17.840 --> 00:43:21.320
But Jenna, first, I want to talk to you about a deleted scene.
不过珍娜，首先我想跟你聊聊一个被删减的片段。

1012
00:43:21.620 --> 00:43:23.520
You will not believe this scene.
你绝对不会相信这个片段。

1013
00:43:23.840 --> 00:43:26.020
I had Sam pull this clip.
我让萨姆把这段剪辑找出来了。

1014
00:43:26.220 --> 00:43:30.680
Jim has called Pam from the road with Michael and Dwight.
吉姆在路上给帕姆打电话，和迈克尔还有德怀特在一起。

1015
00:43:31.220 --> 00:43:38.780
And Pam is kind of passive-aggressively giving Jim a little shade for seeing Karen.
而帕姆有点阴阳怪气地因为吉姆见到凯伦而暗中吃醋。

1016
00:43:39.220 --> 00:43:39.700
Oh.
哦。

1017
00:43:39.920 --> 00:43:42.620
I don't even remember doing this scene.
我都记不得拍过这场戏了。

1018
00:43:42.760 --> 00:43:44.000
I couldn't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

1019
00:43:44.060 --> 00:43:46.040
It just doesn't even sound like Pam to me.
听起来甚至一点都不像帕姆会说的话。

1020
00:43:46.160 --> 00:43:48.580
And I think there's a reason it was deleted.
我想这段被删掉是有原因的。

1021
00:43:48.760 --> 00:43:50.500
But it's pretty delicious to listen to.
不过听起来还挺有意思的。

1022
00:43:50.640 --> 00:43:51.560
Sam, can you play it?
萨姆，能放一下吗？

1023
00:43:52.640 --> 00:43:54.300
Wait, you're going along with this now?
等等，你现在也顺着他胡闹了？

1024
00:43:54.540 --> 00:43:55.220
I have to.
我没办法。

1025
00:43:55.760 --> 00:43:58.720
Pam, if I'm not there, someone's going to go to jail or die.
帕姆，我要是不去，有人就要坐牢或者送命了。

1026
00:43:59.400 --> 00:43:59.880
Right.
对啊。

1027
00:44:00.360 --> 00:44:02.100
And you wouldn't be able to talk to Karen.
而且你就没法跟凯伦说话了。

1028
00:44:02.420 --> 00:44:04.520
Well, I promise you that has nothing to do with it.
我向你保证，这完全没关系。

1029
00:44:04.760 --> 00:44:05.380
A little bit.
有一点吧。

1030
00:44:05.780 --> 00:44:08.520
Well, yeah, I don't want to see her get physically harmed, that's for sure.
好吧，对，我可不想看她受到人身伤害，那是一定的。

1031
00:44:08.700 --> 00:44:09.620
Because you love her?
因为你爱她？

1032
00:44:09.780 --> 00:44:10.960
Because you love her very much?
因为你非常爱她？

1033
00:44:11.020 --> 00:44:11.860
All right, I'm going to go now.
好了，我要挂了。

1034
00:44:12.040 --> 00:44:13.180
Okay, have fun with your girlfriend.
好啊，祝你和你的女朋友玩得开心。

1035
00:44:13.780 --> 00:44:14.540
Okay, I will.
好的，我会的。

1036
00:44:15.500 --> 00:44:15.820
Huh?
啊？

1037
00:44:16.460 --> 00:44:21.120
I mean, Jenna, you're going to have fun with your little girlfriend?
我是说，珍娜，你准备和你的小女朋友玩得开心吗？

1038
00:44:21.500 --> 00:44:23.320
Oh my gosh, Pam is totally jealous.
我的天哪，帕姆完全吃醋了。

1039
00:44:23.820 --> 00:44:24.740
I don't know.
我不知道。

1040
00:44:24.900 --> 00:44:25.980
Do you think she's really jealous?
你觉得她真的吃醋了吗？

1041
00:44:26.340 --> 00:44:26.660
Yes.
是的。

1042
00:44:26.780 --> 00:44:30.040
Pam also has a talking head where she's like, I was just kidding.
帕姆还有一个单人访谈镜头，里面她大概说，我只是开玩笑。

1043
00:44:30.180 --> 00:44:30.820
We kid like that.
我们平时就这么开玩笑。

1044
00:44:30.920 --> 00:44:32.500
And then she's like, okay, maybe I'm a little jealous.
然后她又说，好吧，也许我是吃了一点醋。

1045
00:44:32.900 --> 00:44:33.300
Wow.
哇。

1046
00:44:33.300 --> 00:44:35.140
I don't even remember shooting that.
我甚至不记得拍过那个。

1047
00:44:35.380 --> 00:44:35.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1048
00:44:35.700 --> 00:44:36.580
That's so crazy.
太疯狂了。

1049
00:44:36.580 --> 00:44:38.460
You have to watch the deleted scenes.
你必须得看看这些被删减的片段。

1050
00:44:38.700 --> 00:44:43.220
That does sound a little bit like me when I'm being passive aggressive.
当我阴阳怪气的时候，听起来确实有点像我。

1051
00:44:44.480 --> 00:44:46.200
That was more Jenna than Pam.
那更像是珍娜而不是帕姆。

1052
00:44:46.520 --> 00:44:47.380
Maybe a little bit.
也许有一点吧。

1053
00:44:47.600 --> 00:44:52.720
I think it's good that they deleted it because I think I like instead, you know, that he comes
我觉得他们删掉这个挺好的，因为我更喜欢，你知道的，他最后还是回

1054
00:44:52.720 --> 00:44:54.960
back at the end of the day and, you know, I don't know.
来了，而且，你知道的，我不知道。

1055
00:44:55.040 --> 00:44:56.620
I don't want to see that side of Pam.
我不想看到帕姆的那一面。

1056
00:44:57.140 --> 00:45:00.520
Yeah, I just don't think we need that tension in the relationship.
对，我只是觉得我们不需要这段关系里有那种紧张感。

1057
00:45:00.520 --> 00:45:02.660
It doesn't need to be about that, you know?
没必要扯到那些，你知道吗？

1058
00:45:02.900 --> 00:45:03.140
Yeah.
对。

1059
00:45:03.140 --> 00:45:07.760
I like it and we'll get to it that Jim and Karen are going to have a moment where they
我很喜欢——我们待会儿会聊到——吉姆和凯伦会有一个必须去

1060
00:45:07.760 --> 00:45:08.980
have to deal with their stuff.
处理他们之间问题的时刻。

1061
00:45:08.980 --> 00:45:11.140
But I like that Pam is left out of it.
但我喜欢帕姆没有被卷进去。

1062
00:45:11.480 --> 00:45:12.000
Yeah, me too.
对，我也是。

1063
00:45:12.400 --> 00:45:16.960
So now the guys roll up to the Utica branch and Michael reveals their plan.
所以现在这几个家伙开车到了尤蒂卡分公司，迈克尔透露了他们的计划。

1064
00:45:17.560 --> 00:45:21.640
They're going to pretend to be warehouse workers and they're going to silly string the whole
他们打算假装成仓库工人，然后用彩带喷雾把整个

1065
00:45:21.640 --> 00:45:22.120
place.
地方喷个遍。

1066
00:45:22.560 --> 00:45:27.980
Dwight adds that he might stab the security guy in the eye with a piece of jumbo chalk.
德怀特补充说，他可能会用一块超大号粉笔戳保安的眼睛。

1067
00:45:28.380 --> 00:45:31.580
And Jim is like, you're not stabbing anyone in the eye.
然后吉姆就说，你谁的眼睛都不会戳。

1068
00:45:32.040 --> 00:45:33.160
Dwight's like, okay, fine.
德怀特就说，好吧，行。

1069
00:45:33.280 --> 00:45:35.660
Maybe I'll just grind it up and blow it in his eyes.
也许我把它磨碎了吹进他眼睛里总行吧。

1070
00:45:36.300 --> 00:45:41.860
Yeah, he has a talking head that he says the eyes are the groin of the head.
对，他有一个单人访谈，说眼睛就是脑袋的腹股沟。

1071
00:45:42.260 --> 00:45:42.560
Yeah.
对。

1072
00:45:42.920 --> 00:45:45.340
So look out, eyeballs of Dwight's around.
所以小心了，德怀特出没的地方，眼球们注意了。

1073
00:45:45.620 --> 00:45:47.160
I really love that line.
我真的很喜欢那句台词。

1074
00:45:47.600 --> 00:45:48.260
I did too.
我也很喜欢。

1075
00:45:48.840 --> 00:45:53.300
Dwight and Michael leave and Jim is now on a walkie-talkie in the car.
德怀特和迈克尔走了，吉姆现在在车里用对讲机。

1076
00:45:53.540 --> 00:45:54.840
Well, and he sees Karen.
嗯，然后他看到了凯伦。

1077
00:45:55.140 --> 00:45:56.100
He's like, oh my God, she's here.
他就像是，天哪，她在这儿。

1078
00:45:56.180 --> 00:45:56.640
Go, go, go.
快，快，快。

1079
00:45:56.800 --> 00:46:00.360
And he leans the seat back trying to hide from Karen.
然后他把座位往后放倒，试图躲开凯伦。

1080
00:46:00.360 --> 00:46:01.020
Yeah.
对。

1081
00:46:01.240 --> 00:46:06.540
But in the meantime, through the walkie-talkie, we only hear it, which I personally think
但与此同时，通过对讲机，我们只能听到声音，我个人觉得

1082
00:46:06.540 --> 00:46:07.840
is so freaking funny.
这简直太搞笑了吧。

1083
00:46:08.260 --> 00:46:11.400
Michael and Dwight decide to steal the industrial copier.
迈克尔和德怀特决定偷走那台工业复印机。

1084
00:46:11.600 --> 00:46:14.840
Then you hear a very loud crashing noise.
然后你听到了非常大的一声巨响。

1085
00:46:15.200 --> 00:46:19.600
And then you start to hear Michael talking about his hip.
接着你开始听到迈克尔在说他的臀部。

1086
00:46:20.100 --> 00:46:21.960
He's saying, Jim, save us.
他在喊，吉姆，救救我们。

1087
00:46:22.520 --> 00:46:27.140
He's saying, Jim, if this is my last moment, please tell me you'll take over the Dundies.
他在喊，吉姆，如果这是我的最后时刻，请答应我你会接管邓迪奖。

1088
00:46:27.880 --> 00:46:30.600
It's so, so amazing.
这真的是太、太棒了。

1089
00:46:31.100 --> 00:46:32.700
And Jenna, you're so right.
